"For each item below, fetch its source and check that the recorded quote appears on the page and supports the item. A card item is a field of the plan in the producer's words, with the sources it cites: check each factual claim in it against those sources, and any value it carries against the page; what the plan will build, measure or predict needs no source, but a factual claim with no source is UNSUPPORTED. For a cost input, check that the page states the number for the setting given; whether it applies to this plan is not yours to judge. When the page states a different number for a num or rate item, give it as page_value. Decide only from the pages you fetch and the text below; do not read files. Return one status per item, under its ref: SUPPORTED, PARTIAL, UNSUPPORTED, CONTRADICTED or UNREACHABLE, with the page sentence you relied on.
Items, one per line:
{\"ref\":\"card:question\",\"text\":\"Does molecular-dynamics verification of viscosity and thermal conductivity reorder a machine-learning ester shortlist, or merely confirm it, and does the best coolant keep improving?\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"card:hypothesis\",\"text\":\"Molecular dynamics will reorder the shortlist because the machine-learning viscosity error (22.5% MAPE) exceeds MD's, so better esters appear only after verification.\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"card:sequential_part\",\"text\":\"Each candidate's viscosity waits on one long trajectory; the ranking waits on 100, 300, then 1000 candidates.\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"card:method\",\"text\":\"Run each candidate as parallel short replicas on separate GPUs and block-average the Green-Kubo integrals, so wall-clock shrinks by the replica count.\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"card:if_lever\",\"text\":\"By 100 candidates the replica ranking matches the sequential baseline and diverges from ML; the best figure keeps improving through 1000.\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"card:if_not\",\"text\":\"Replicas only match the sequential baseline by 300 candidates, and MD then merely confirms the ML ranking, unchanged from 100 through 1000.\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"card:test_summary\",\"text\":\"Rent an 8-GPU A100 node; run OPLS-AA Green-Kubo viscosity and thermal conductivity for the top 100 then 300 of Org-Mol's 461 monoesters; compare ML-vs-MD rank correlation and whether the best cooling figure keeps climbing; time a 45 ns single-trajectory baseline against parallel 5 ns replicas.\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"card:closest_prior\",\"text\":\"Org-Mol screened 461 monoester cooling candidates with a transformer and measured only two by synthesis; none were molecular-dynamics-verified for viscosity or thermal conductivity [s1].\",\"sources\":[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"url\":\"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41524-025-01720-4\",\"quote\":\"Based on the aforementioned criteria of the kinematic viscosity and thermal conductivity, 461 monoesters are finally filtered out.\"}],\"value\":0}
{\"ref\":\"card:left_open\",\"text\":\"No published work runs Green-Kubo viscosity and thermal conductivity over a 100-to-1000 candidate ester shortlist, so whether MD reorders the ML ranking is untested.\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"card:anchor\",\"text\":\"Green-Kubo MD (OPLS-AA) reproduces Org-Mol Ester 1's measured 40 C viscosity 6.41 cSt\",\"sources\":[{\"id\":\"s3\",\"url\":\"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41524-025-01720-4/tables/4\",\"quote\":\"Ester 1 2.80 3.13 6.41 7.18 1.98 2.23 0.141 0.144\"}],\"value\":6.41}
{\"ref\":\"card:limits\",\"text\":\"Shows single-phase ranking only, under one force field and 15 ns sampling; no synthesis, dielectric, flammability, compatibility, or stability checks.\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"src:s1\",\"url\":\"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41524-025-01720-4\",\"quote\":\"Based on the aforementioned criteria of the kinematic viscosity and thermal conductivity, 461 monoesters are finally filtered out.\",\"supports\":\"the 461-candidate shortlist the MD step is inserted into (baseline).\"}
{\"ref\":\"src:s3\",\"url\":\"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41524-025-01720-4/tables/4\",\"quote\":\"Ester 1 2.80 3.13 6.41 7.18 1.98 2.23 0.141 0.144\",\"supports\":\"anchor: Ester 1 measured kinematic viscosity at 40 C = 6.41 cSt and thermal conductivity = 0.141 W/m K.\"}
{\"ref\":\"num:a100_ns_day\",\"name\":\"GROMACS throughput on A100 for a 20,000-atom liquid\",\"value\":267.5,\"unit\":\"ns/day\",\"basis\":\"PROXY\",\"quote\":\"| A100 | 267.5 | 691.7 | 265.8 | 129.1 | 38.8 | 23.2 |\",\"page_setting\":\"NHR@FAU GROMACS 2024 benchmark, system 1 (a 20,248-atom liquid).\",\"differs_in\":[\"system: R-143a-in-hexane 20,248 atoms vs a ~20,000-atom saturated monoester box\",\"force field: benchmark AMBER-family vs my OPLS-AA\",\"benchmark has a very high output rate, which the NHR authors note lowers ns/day by ~2.6x vs a low-output run\"],\"url\":\"https://hpc.fau.de/2024/08/13/gromacs-2024-1-on-brand-new-gpgpus/\"}
